 "caveats": [
  "arms share seed 0 and incident ids; a different window changes the state space, so draws decorrelate only partially; z combines the binomial SEMs as if independent",
  "TDS window convergence: r21 vs r25 |z| <= 0.54 on every tally; r17 sits 1-2 sigma high in outgoing at 1e3/1e4 A, so r21 = (15,21) is the converged choice at this precision",
  "mean TDS jump count still rises r21 -> r25 (1.93 -> 2.08, 2.3 sigma without the correlation correction) while every terminal tally is unchanged; open",
  "electronic arms: r17 (1,000) vs r21 (500) |z| <= 1.44; electronic kick harmonics |n| <= 4 truncate rho_q (see kick_truncation); the truncated columns define the model's electronic loss",
  "box (30,42) fixed (reach ~49 A^-1 per axis); box convergence and the out-of-box tail are #882 / #881",
  "the SLURM memory request was lowered from 6G to 4500M for tasks 31-159 while pending (scheduling only; peak RSS <= 1.6 GB)",
  "Gamma retained-state counts from axial_states + gap_cut at the 139.25 eV target; the square M=12 window (y reach 13.9 A^-1) is unconverged (535 vs 655)"
 ],
 "job": {
  "slurm_array": "3158_[0-159%16], partition cpu, 1 CPU/task",
  "sbatch": "#!/bin/bash\n#SBATCH --job-name=fib880\n#SBATCH --partition=cpu\n#SBATCH --ntasks=1\n#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=1\n#SBATCH --mem=6G\n#SBATCH --time=06:00:00\n#SBATCH --output=/home/aamador/pyrite-880/runs/logs/%A_%a.log\nset -euo pipefail\ncd \"$HOME/pyrite-880\"\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\nexport PYRITE_HOME=\"$HOME/pyrite\" PYRITE_CATALOG=\"$PWD/src/pyrite/data/catalog\"\nexport PYRITE_USER_CATALOG=\"$(mktemp -d)/catalog\" XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\nexport OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1\nread -r arm start count < <(sed -n \"$((SLURM_ARRAY_TASK_ID + 1))p\" runs/tasks.txt)\nout=\"runs/out/${arm}-${start}.json\"\n[ -s \"$out\" ] && { echo \"exists $out\"; exit 0; }\nkwargs=$(uv run --no-sync python -c \"import json,sys; print(json.dumps(json.load(open('runs/arms.json'))[sys.argv[1]]))\" \"$arm\")\necho \"sha=$(cat SOURCE_SHA) arm=$arm start=$start count=$count host=$(hostname) kwargs=$kwargs\"\n/usr/bin/time -v uv run --no-sync python checks/axial_outgoing_maps.py fiber-chunk \"$kwargs\" \"$start\" \"$count\" \"$out.tmp\"\nmv \"$out.tmp\" \"$out\"\n",
